export anchor NightVisionStyle:
    number: 302
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Night vision
    idea: The pull request seen through a night vision viewfinder, one phosphor green on black with grain, a vignette, corner readouts and a reticle on the title, so every status speaks through its shape and word.
    base: dark
    palette:
        black: #000000, the page surround
        scopeBlack: #020902, the viewfinder and style sheet ground
        zone: #061406, zones, fields and the comment
        phosphor: #a6ff9e, text, the primary button and the focus halo
        bloom: #d6ffd0, headings, the failing and changes outlines and the focus outline
        phosphorLow: #6fd06a, labels, removed lines and meta
        phosphorDim: #2c6a2a, the reticle and control outlines
        trace: #1f4d1e, zone borders and dashed dividers
        addedGlow: #0b260b, added line ground
    type:
        One monospace family throughout, OCR A Std, OCR-A, Lucida Console,
        ui-monospace, DejaVu Sans Mono, with a soft green text glow. Base
        14px at 1.55. The title is 34px caps, the repository 22px, the
        checks figure 30px, labels 11 to 12px caps tracked 0.12 to 0.16em,
        the diff 12.5px.
    layout:
        The screen is one viewfinder, a black rounded rectangle with a 28px
        radius, faint green grain behind the content and a dark vignette at
        the edges. An on screen readout row shows a ring with Brightwork
        code live, IR 2 and gain, and the channel PR 214. The header holds
        the repository and a Private note, the tabs as caps with a pointer
        before the current one, and outlined counters at the right. A
        dashed rule leads to the target, a centred block with a framed
        Open PR 214 tag, the title in caps and the merge sentence, behind
        which a reticle draws crosshair lines with a gap round the title,
        tick marks and four corner brackets. Below are three zones, 260px,
        flexible and 260px, each a bordered box with a plus before its
        label. Checks shows 11 of 12 and every check with a tick and ok,
        the failing one boxed in a dashed bright outline with an octagon
        cross and failing. The diff zone shows added lines bright on a
        green ground and removed lines dim and struck, with the comment as
        a bright framed Mark joined by a short line. The right zones hold
        reviewers, files with added and removed counts, details and a
        dashed disabled merge. Below 1100px the diff leads.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between zones, 12px zone padding, 48px around the reticle.
    density: Medium. One centred target, then three zones of readouts.
    corners: A 28px rounded viewfinder, 4px buttons and fields, square zones.
    borders: 1px trace green on zones, dashed dividers, and a dashed bloom outline on whatever fails.
    shadows: A soft green text glow and a dark vignette at the viewfinder edge, with grain behind the content.
    icons:
        1.8px line icons in the one green. A tick for passed, an octagon
        cross for failing, a ringed tick for approved, a triangle for
        changes, always with the word, since colour cannot help.
    focus: A 2px bloom outline offset 3px with a 6px phosphor halo.
    tone: Camera readouts, such as Live, IR 2, Gain, Mark and Locked until all checks pass.
